1
00:00:12,958 --> 00:00:14,125
(Ryu Se-il)

2
00:00:20,333 --> 00:00:22,042
(Ha Jung-hoon)

3
00:00:27,792 --> 00:00:29,417
(Lee Jung-chan)

4
00:00:34,875 --> 00:00:36,625
(Jung Si-wan)

5
00:00:44,917 --> 00:00:46,708
"Boy, with Caution"

6
00:00:51,750 --> 00:00:54,518
(Don't you even know what affection is?) Any
kind of emotion must feel pretty dull to you.

7
00:00:54,542 --> 00:00:56,250
Because that's just who I am.

8
00:00:59,083 --> 00:01:00,417
That's not true.

9
00:01:02,833 --> 00:01:04,292
Sir.

10
00:01:13,167 --> 00:01:15,792
I wouldn't delude myself
about someone so dull.

11
00:01:21,083 --> 00:01:27,125
So can I... keep deluding myself?

12
00:01:30,250 --> 00:01:32,750
"Boy, with Caution"
(Episode 4)

13
00:01:32,875 --> 00:01:35,708
Why do you think you're dull?

14
00:01:49,333 --> 00:01:50,792
(Jung Soo-bin)

15
00:01:54,750 --> 00:01:57,550
Was there really something going
on between you and that Soo-bin girl?

16
00:01:57,792 --> 00:02:00,167
Ji-young, let's talk.

17
00:02:00,292 --> 00:02:01,292
Can we please talk?

18
00:02:02,333 --> 00:02:03,976
You know that's not true.
Why are you so upset?

19
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:06,708
If it isn't, then why are you
still working as a substitute teacher?

20
00:02:06,833 --> 00:02:09,018
Didn't you say you'd take the certification
exam for a permanent position?

21
00:02:09,042 --> 00:02:10,934
You're way past the age to be
bouncing around as a contract teacher.

22
00:02:10,958 --> 00:02:12,750
Because I haven't...

23
00:02:13,708 --> 00:02:14,917
I'm not ready yet.

24
00:02:15,708 --> 00:02:16,976
That student already dropped out.

25
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:18,292
Did you know that?

26
00:02:18,542 --> 00:02:21,375
She just couldn't take the rumors anymore.

27
00:02:21,500 --> 00:02:23,917
She dropped out on her own
because of the humiliation.

28
00:02:24,333 --> 00:02:26,053
You said it wasn't even that big of a deal!

29
00:02:26,083 --> 00:02:28,625
I acted like that precisely
because it wasn't!

30
00:02:30,750 --> 00:02:32,208
I know all too well

31
00:02:32,833 --> 00:02:34,458
what really happened.

32
00:02:38,042 --> 00:02:39,083
Fine.

33
00:02:39,917 --> 00:02:42,542
If you think it's that
serious, suit yourself.

34
00:02:43,333 --> 00:02:44,875
But Gi-woo,

35
00:02:46,875 --> 00:02:49,458
I really can't stand you
being dull like this anymore.

36
00:02:51,583 --> 00:02:53,750
It's driving me insane.

37
00:02:54,583 --> 00:02:55,958
Do you get that?

38
00:02:57,542 --> 00:02:59,375
I'm staying at my mom's place for a while.

39
00:03:08,292 --> 00:03:10,167
You're special to me, Sir.

40
00:03:23,500 --> 00:03:25,250
What brings you here out of the blue?

41
00:03:26,333 --> 00:03:29,042
I was making kimchi and
ended up making too much.

42
00:03:29,167 --> 00:03:30,458
I'm exhausted.

43
00:03:30,583 --> 00:03:33,417
I tried calling Ji-young,
but she wouldn't answer.

44
00:03:34,458 --> 00:03:35,333
What are you just standing there for?

45
00:03:35,458 --> 00:03:37,208
Go wash your hands and let's eat.

46
00:03:52,292 --> 00:03:53,583
You're having a drink?

47
00:03:53,708 --> 00:03:55,417
A little drink goes well with a meal.

48
00:03:55,542 --> 00:03:57,083
Want a glass too?

49
00:03:57,917 --> 00:03:59,125
No, I'm fine.

50
00:04:04,875 --> 00:04:06,125
Where's Ji-young?

51
00:04:07,708 --> 00:04:09,167
She went to work.

52
00:04:09,667 --> 00:04:10,958
Isn't it the weekend?

53
00:04:11,875 --> 00:04:14,083
Did you come over to
check if Ji-young was home?

54
00:04:15,833 --> 00:04:17,633
I was worried she was
avoiding me on purpose.

55
00:04:18,833 --> 00:04:22,542
You two aren't breaking up, are you?

56
00:04:25,292 --> 00:04:26,542
Are you?

57
00:04:32,042 --> 00:04:33,542
Of course not.

58
00:04:33,667 --> 00:04:36,307
She had to go on an overseas
business trip and forgot to tell you.

59
00:04:37,542 --> 00:04:39,208
Ah, give me your bowl.

60
00:05:00,208 --> 00:05:02,083
Don't break up.

61
00:05:02,208 --> 00:05:04,042
Mom is begging you.

62
00:05:06,250 --> 00:05:11,042
If word gets out, people will think
there's something wrong with you.

63
00:05:18,750 --> 00:05:22,167
I don't want to be dull anymore.

64
00:05:33,667 --> 00:05:35,625
But I don't know what
to do [to change that].

65
00:05:36,875 --> 00:05:39,000
(Teacher Certification Exam Study Guide)

66
00:05:42,417 --> 00:05:44,500
(Teacher Certification Exam Schedule)

67
00:05:47,333 --> 00:05:48,893
And I don't have the confidence either.

68
00:05:59,167 --> 00:06:01,917
Because I've always tried so hard
not to be seen as defective.

69
00:06:28,542 --> 00:06:31,458
So I didn't know how
to react with the word...

70
00:06:34,667 --> 00:06:35,917
"special."

71
00:06:36,458 --> 00:06:38,750
(I didn't know how to react)

72
00:06:57,000 --> 00:06:59,667
Then how did you feel in that moment?

73
00:06:59,792 --> 00:07:01,292
That's what matters most.

74
00:07:06,208 --> 00:07:08,667
Choi Young-moon. Gold Prize.

75
00:07:08,792 --> 00:07:13,583
For placing first in the 2026 In-School
Mathematics Competition,

76
00:07:13,708 --> 00:07:15,108
this certificate is hereby awarded.

77
00:07:17,500 --> 00:07:18,750
Awesome.

78
00:07:21,542 --> 00:07:23,708
Park Sung-won. Silver Prize.

79
00:07:23,833 --> 00:07:25,208
Same as above.

80
00:07:39,833 --> 00:07:41,083
Class dismissed.

81
00:07:55,500 --> 00:07:56,708
Hyeon-jae.

82
00:07:59,208 --> 00:08:01,888
It's time for your career counseling.
Come to the teachers' office.

83
00:08:07,458 --> 00:08:10,018
(Nagwon High School Career Counseling Form)
Desired University: None. Career Goal: None.

84
00:08:10,042 --> 00:08:13,208
Reason: Believes everything
ends after graduation.

85
00:08:18,000 --> 00:08:19,480
Does everything end after graduation?

86
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:24,667
- Yes.
- What ends?

87
00:08:25,333 --> 00:08:26,875
Are you saying you want to die?

88
00:08:28,500 --> 00:08:30,125
Is this your way of handling things?

89
00:08:32,250 --> 00:08:35,000
Doing this just to get attention?

90
00:08:38,958 --> 00:08:40,417
You're not gonna answer?

91
00:08:43,917 --> 00:08:46,667
It's not like you actually
care about my answer, Sir.

92
00:08:51,375 --> 00:08:55,583
You've been deliberately harsh
with your words the entire time.

93
00:08:57,083 --> 00:08:59,458
If this is about what I said last time...

94
00:09:01,958 --> 00:09:03,583
I'm sorry.

95
00:09:04,667 --> 00:09:06,250
I made a mistake.

96
00:09:11,333 --> 00:09:13,000
I'm nobody special anyway.

97
00:09:17,042 --> 00:09:21,625
What I'm saying is, don't
read too much into it.

98
00:09:23,542 --> 00:09:25,167
What I think is my business.

99
00:09:29,583 --> 00:09:30,917
You may go.

100
00:09:48,542 --> 00:09:49,917
(Sunflower - Message)

101
00:09:50,042 --> 00:09:52,125
You could have just accepted it.

102
00:09:53,958 --> 00:09:56,583
Accept that you could actually
be special to someone.

103
00:09:58,625 --> 00:09:59,667
Hyeon-jae.

104
00:10:02,125 --> 00:10:04,917
Whose idea was that counseling session?

105
00:10:05,042 --> 00:10:06,625
Is there a problem?

106
00:10:08,417 --> 00:10:09,417
Not at all.

107
00:10:09,500 --> 00:10:10,792
Are you sure?

108
00:10:14,542 --> 00:10:15,976
If you're heading to the chairman's office,

109
00:10:16,000 --> 00:10:17,583
let's walk down together.

110
00:10:20,667 --> 00:10:23,250
Aren't you supposed to
see your mother today?

111
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:33,917
Please get changed and
come out. I'll wait outside.

112
00:10:34,042 --> 00:10:35,875
Don't you owe me an explanation first?

113
00:10:37,625 --> 00:10:39,375
Why do I suddenly need to see my mother?

114
00:10:39,500 --> 00:10:42,208
The chairman has business and
will be stopping by the hospital.

115
00:10:44,000 --> 00:10:46,375
Is it personal or school business?

116
00:10:48,042 --> 00:10:49,625
This suit looks good on you.

117
00:10:50,542 --> 00:10:51,833
I'm not going.

118
00:10:53,750 --> 00:10:56,375
We must arrive by two. Please hurry.

119
00:10:56,500 --> 00:10:57,833
I said I'm not going!

120
00:10:57,958 --> 00:11:01,278
Do you still want to be able to see your
mother at the hospital after you graduate?

121
00:11:01,958 --> 00:11:03,792
Is that how you talked to my mom too?

122
00:11:03,917 --> 00:11:05,042
No.

123
00:11:08,708 --> 00:11:10,958
Only because you refuse to cooperate.

124
00:11:12,583 --> 00:11:14,083
Please be out in ten minutes.

125
00:11:16,625 --> 00:11:18,458
How much longer...

126
00:11:21,542 --> 00:11:22,958
do I have to put up with this crap?

127
00:11:24,625 --> 00:11:25,958
Who knows?

128
00:11:27,875 --> 00:11:31,083
That's why you should live quietly
and pretend you don't even exist,

129
00:11:31,208 --> 00:11:32,875
just as agreed.

130
00:11:36,083 --> 00:11:39,000
If the bill isn't paid, the
transfer cannot be processed.

131
00:11:46,125 --> 00:11:48,458
Please select your transaction.

132
00:11:48,583 --> 00:11:52,458
(Credit Card Cash Advance)
Please select your transaction.

133
00:11:56,958 --> 00:11:58,558
(Transaction Failed: Insufficient Funds)

134
00:12:02,250 --> 00:12:04,958
Is he crazy?

135
00:12:05,083 --> 00:12:06,625
He's completely out of his mind.

136
00:12:06,750 --> 00:12:08,000
Where's the rest of the money?

137
00:12:08,958 --> 00:12:09,708
Oh, you made it?

138
00:12:09,833 --> 00:12:12,042
I thought Lee Hyeon-jae
beat the crap out of you

139
00:12:12,167 --> 00:12:14,167
and you were too humiliated to show up.

140
00:12:15,125 --> 00:12:16,458
Give me the payment.

141
00:12:17,000 --> 00:12:18,542
I held up my end, didn't I?

142
00:12:21,000 --> 00:12:23,333
What, did Lee Hyeon-jae
mess you up that badly?

143
00:12:24,292 --> 00:12:27,458
Guess you can't even play
the vending machine anymore.

144
00:12:30,042 --> 00:12:32,917
Hey, don't you have Ji Tae-hyeong's card?

145
00:12:35,667 --> 00:12:40,250
If you're broke, go take out
a loan. Why the sour face?

146
00:12:43,542 --> 00:12:44,792
(Loan Inquiries)

147
00:12:50,000 --> 00:12:52,750
I'll let him know in
advance. Go talk to him.

148
00:12:53,125 --> 00:12:56,375
He loves kids like you.

149
00:13:24,375 --> 00:13:25,917
Hyeon-jong, got a problem?

150
00:13:27,375 --> 00:13:30,458
I took time out of my day to give
you some cardio. What's with that look?

151
00:13:32,167 --> 00:13:33,583
I'll try one more time.

152
00:13:37,542 --> 00:13:40,862
If you ever give me lip again with some
bullshit excuse about not having collateral,

153
00:13:43,250 --> 00:13:46,750
I'm going after your parents. You hear me?

154
00:13:47,625 --> 00:13:49,000
Keep that in mind.

155
00:13:50,750 --> 00:13:52,375
Why aren't you answering?

156
00:13:52,500 --> 00:13:55,917
No, I understand.

157
00:13:57,083 --> 00:13:57,875
I really do.

158
00:13:58,000 --> 00:14:00,292
You're not deaf, so of
course you understand.

159
00:14:02,375 --> 00:14:04,000
You know I used to be an athlete, right?

160
00:14:04,875 --> 00:14:06,315
Useless punks like you make me sick.

161
00:14:06,375 --> 00:14:08,333
Moving slow as hell. It pisses me off.

162
00:14:10,250 --> 00:14:11,667
So watch yourself.

163
00:14:12,250 --> 00:14:13,292
Yes, sir.

164
00:14:14,250 --> 00:14:15,583
I'm sorry.

165
00:14:25,542 --> 00:14:26,958
Here for a loan?

166
00:14:30,875 --> 00:14:32,542
So you're the vending machine?

167
00:14:32,667 --> 00:14:33,958
Choi Young-moon's lackey?

168
00:14:37,708 --> 00:14:39,958
Where does he score those pills?

169
00:14:40,625 --> 00:14:42,250
Can't you just tell me that?

170
00:14:48,542 --> 00:14:52,292
Begging everywhere for cash—what took you so
long? Pick better people to run errands for.

171
00:14:52,417 --> 00:14:55,292
But Choi Young-moon's
even sending his dirty work...

172
00:14:57,667 --> 00:15:01,833
Is totally spineless, isn't it?

173
00:15:03,625 --> 00:15:05,042
Just kidding.

174
00:15:06,458 --> 00:15:08,309
Who cares about pride when
you're borrowing money?

175
00:15:08,333 --> 00:15:09,583
Right?

176
00:15:18,208 --> 00:15:19,792
I don't smoke.

177
00:15:20,833 --> 00:15:22,125
Why not?

178
00:15:22,250 --> 00:15:23,458
Because I'm an athlete.

179
00:15:23,583 --> 00:15:26,503
I've never seen anyone built like you
who was actually any good at sports.

180
00:15:32,125 --> 00:15:34,917
It's not like you'll ever go pro anyway.
Have one.

181
00:15:57,208 --> 00:16:00,125
So, how much do you need?

182
00:16:00,458 --> 00:16:02,208
- Ten million won.
- That was quick.

183
00:16:08,250 --> 00:16:09,417
What about collateral?

184
00:16:19,000 --> 00:16:21,542
If you don't have anything to put up,

185
00:16:22,458 --> 00:16:24,218
do you want to offer
yourself as collateral?

186
00:16:28,333 --> 00:16:30,375
Did something happen today?

187
00:16:31,417 --> 00:16:33,177
You haven't said a word.
(Sunflower Chatroom)

188
00:16:34,417 --> 00:16:36,537
(Did something happen
today? You haven't said a word)

189
00:16:45,792 --> 00:16:48,875
(Lee Hyeon-jae - Incoming Call)

190
00:16:54,125 --> 00:16:55,875
Hello?

191
00:16:58,583 --> 00:17:00,000
Hello?

192
00:17:03,250 --> 00:17:04,708
Lee Hyeon-jae.

193
00:17:05,167 --> 00:17:06,500
Yes, Sir.

194
00:17:06,958 --> 00:17:08,758
Why call if you're not
going to say anything?

195
00:17:09,083 --> 00:17:10,333
Sir.

196
00:17:12,125 --> 00:17:13,958
I was fine before.

197
00:17:16,542 --> 00:17:18,302
Living like I didn't
exist didn't bother me.

198
00:17:18,583 --> 00:17:20,583
(Mr. Jang Gi-woo)

199
00:17:20,708 --> 00:17:22,583
But I can't do it anymore.

200
00:17:25,208 --> 00:17:27,417
I can't hold out any longer.

201
00:17:31,375 --> 00:17:32,792
Where are you right now?

202
00:17:35,375 --> 00:17:37,458
If I tell you, will you come?

203
00:17:40,125 --> 00:17:41,542
Will you come to me?

204
00:17:43,083 --> 00:17:46,125
I'll head over right now. Where are you?

205
00:17:47,542 --> 00:17:48,875
At school.

206
00:17:51,667 --> 00:17:54,917
Did you eat dinner?

207
00:18:12,833 --> 00:18:14,250
Want to order more?

208
00:18:14,875 --> 00:18:16,667
Sir, you've barely touched your food.

209
00:18:18,292 --> 00:18:20,125
I just noticed you weren't eating much.

210
00:18:22,458 --> 00:18:24,167
I had a bite for lunch but...

211
00:18:25,167 --> 00:18:26,647
I was uncomfortable [the whole time].

212
00:18:28,333 --> 00:18:29,917
I can tell.

213
00:18:32,667 --> 00:18:34,333
I mean, you look uncomfortable.

214
00:18:41,000 --> 00:18:43,833
Eat up. We can always order more.

215
00:18:56,042 --> 00:18:58,402
How do you pretend you don't
exist when you're right there?

216
00:19:01,250 --> 00:19:03,125
That's what I hear most often.

217
00:19:04,750 --> 00:19:10,333
Sometimes I think I understand, but other
times, I'm completely lost with what that means.

218
00:19:11,917 --> 00:19:13,375
Then stop dwelling on it.

219
00:19:22,750 --> 00:19:24,958
I've been wrecking myself on purpose

220
00:19:27,458 --> 00:19:29,500
just to make everyone
around me feel ashamed.

221
00:19:31,958 --> 00:19:35,167
I wanted to be the only stain
on my father's pristine life.

222
00:19:41,167 --> 00:19:42,333
Sir.

223
00:19:44,500 --> 00:19:49,417
I can't crash at your
place tonight... right?

224
00:19:54,333 --> 00:19:55,750
You know you can't, so why ask?

225
00:20:01,292 --> 00:20:03,208
I was just putting it out there.

226
00:20:05,167 --> 00:20:06,375
Could I get a Coke, please?

227
00:20:06,500 --> 00:20:08,042
Sure, right away.

228
00:20:13,833 --> 00:20:16,833
Do you have a friend who can cover for you
and say you're staying the night?

229
00:20:21,542 --> 00:20:24,022
I have to walk on eggshells
around the chairman too, you know.

230
00:20:30,125 --> 00:20:31,458
I do.

231
00:20:31,583 --> 00:20:33,292
This is about your dad, isn't it?

232
00:20:45,167 --> 00:20:46,417
Just this once.

233
00:20:56,208 --> 00:20:57,500
Honey, you're back?

234
00:20:57,625 --> 00:20:58,958
I heard Mom came over.

235
00:20:59,083 --> 00:21:01,163
Didn't I tell you to call
me if you needed anything?

236
00:21:05,625 --> 00:21:07,000
You have company?

237
00:21:12,375 --> 00:21:13,542
Is he a student?

238
00:21:18,042 --> 00:21:19,875
Are you actually out of your mind?

239
00:21:20,000 --> 00:21:22,333
Didn't I tell you I'd be home today?

240
00:21:23,333 --> 00:21:26,125
You didn't even remember again, did you?

241
00:21:26,792 --> 00:21:28,917
He's a Nagwon High student, isn't he?

242
00:21:29,042 --> 00:21:31,333
Bringing him home... what are you doing?

243
00:21:32,000 --> 00:21:33,833
Is your place a youth shelter now?

244
00:21:34,833 --> 00:21:36,292
I have my reasons.

245
00:21:36,417 --> 00:21:38,625
When don't you have an excuse?

246
00:21:53,750 --> 00:21:57,958
Didn't I tell you
to call me whenever you see Mom?

247
00:21:58,083 --> 00:22:01,667
Mom called asking if we broke up.

248
00:22:01,792 --> 00:22:03,542
Care to guess what I said?

249
00:22:05,750 --> 00:22:07,250
She already knows.

250
00:22:08,208 --> 00:22:09,267
What?

251
00:22:09,292 --> 00:22:13,917
She knows, but she's just
waiting for me to say it first.

252
00:22:15,167 --> 00:22:19,250
Just like before, avoiding it.

253
00:22:24,000 --> 00:22:25,750
And you think you aren't running away?

254
00:22:29,167 --> 00:22:30,542
And another thing, Gi-woo.

255
00:22:31,958 --> 00:22:34,708
Either see things through to the
end, or stay out of it completely.

256
00:22:35,833 --> 00:22:37,792
Whether it's your mother, me,

257
00:22:37,917 --> 00:22:39,333
or that student of yours.

258
00:22:49,583 --> 00:22:51,083
Hand me my bag.

259
00:22:51,208 --> 00:22:53,667
Thanks to your guest, I haven't
even had the chance to pack.

260
00:22:55,333 --> 00:22:56,500
Hello?

261
00:22:57,875 --> 00:22:59,125
Yes, Producer.

262
00:23:00,708 --> 00:23:01,958
Right now?

263
00:23:06,167 --> 00:23:09,083
Right now is a bit tough.

264
00:23:11,833 --> 00:23:14,417
I can make it in about forty minutes.

265
00:23:31,125 --> 00:23:32,208
Sir.

266
00:23:35,000 --> 00:23:37,250
Have you had students like me before?

267
00:23:45,833 --> 00:23:47,208
Students you gave special care to?

268
00:23:49,417 --> 00:23:51,208
Are you like this with everyone?

269
00:23:55,542 --> 00:23:57,125
How much of that did you hear?

270
00:24:05,167 --> 00:24:06,542
I'm stepping out for a minute.

271
00:24:17,625 --> 00:24:20,542
Which place among them am I to you, Sir?

272
00:24:23,042 --> 00:24:23,917
Let go.

273
00:24:24,042 --> 00:24:27,042
Why won't you answer me?

274
00:24:41,458 --> 00:24:43,098
What difference does it make if you know?

275
00:24:49,500 --> 00:24:51,583
Did you treat them like this too?

276
00:24:53,542 --> 00:24:55,875
Patching them up when they got beaten?

277
00:24:56,458 --> 00:24:58,738
Letting them spend the night
when they had nowhere to go?

278
00:25:31,708 --> 00:25:33,167
I...

279
00:25:36,417 --> 00:25:39,708
I want to be your only one.

280
00:25:44,625 --> 00:25:46,083
Just like you are to me.

281
00:26:19,125 --> 00:26:20,875
Boy, with Caution.

282
00:26:21,792 --> 00:26:23,226
(Coming Up)
Did I do something wrong?

283
00:26:23,250 --> 00:26:24,792
I really don't understand.

284
00:26:24,917 --> 00:26:26,750
How can having feelings
for someone be wrong?

285
00:26:26,875 --> 00:26:27,750
Did you do that on purpose?

286
00:26:27,875 --> 00:26:30,208
Otherwise, you'd just pretend
nothing ever happened.

287
00:26:30,458 --> 00:26:31,667
Take it off.

288
00:26:31,792 --> 00:26:33,312
It's/You're too pretty. This won't do.

289
00:26:34,208 --> 00:26:34,958
Talk to me.

290
00:26:35,083 --> 00:26:36,292
Let's talk later.

291
00:26:37,000 --> 00:26:38,583
Think whatever you want.

292
00:26:38,708 --> 00:26:39,583
Lee Hyeon-jae?

293
00:26:39,708 --> 00:26:41,000
Long time no see.

294
00:26:43,542 --> 00:26:44,917
Where is Ji Tae-hyeong?

295
00:26:46,000 --> 00:26:47,375
You must be "Regret," right?
